{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "47050a02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Building Defect AI — Notebook workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "Run from the repository root. Expected data layout: `dataset/BD3_split/{train,val,test}/<class_name>/...`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** classify images into the seven BD3 labels. This notebook records the method, why it is used, the result and its interpretation. Do not treat model predictions as professional inspection findings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5baf7ba8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets, models\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "DATA = ROOT / \"dataset\" / \"BD3_split\"\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(\"Project:\", ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Device:\", DEVICE)\n",
    "assert DATA.exists(), f\"Dataset folder not found: {DATA}. Run from the project root and add the dataset.\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "476eac93",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Transfer learning setup\n",
    "\n",
    "ResNet18 is a convolutional neural network pretrained on ImageNet. We replace its final fully connected layer with a seven-class classifier. First train only the new classifier; then selectively unfreeze deeper layers. This compares adaptation capacity against overfitting risk.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a reproducible training baseline. The recorded project experiments remain in `original_scripts/`; do not overwrite the published Experiment 3 checkpoint until a new run has been validated."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "44295964",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import copy\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n",
    "weights = models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT\n",
    "tfm = weights.transforms()\n",
    "train_ds = datasets.ImageFolder(DATA / \"train\", transform=tfm)\n",
    "val_ds = datasets.ImageFolder(DATA / \"val\", transform=tfm)\n",
    "assert train_ds.classes == val_ds.classes\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=16, shuffle=True, num_workers=0)\n",
    "val_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=16, shuffle=False, num_workers=0)\n",
    "model = models.resnet18(weights=weights)\n",
    "model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, len(train_ds.classes))\n",
    "for p in model.parameters(): p.requires_grad = False\n",
    "for p in model.fc.parameters(): p.requires_grad = True\n",
    "model = model.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
    "optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.fc.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n",
    "print(\"Trainable parameters:\", sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa9d60e6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Train classifier head\n",
    "\n",
    "Cross entropy is the standard objective for mutually exclusive classes. Adam updates the trainable classifier weights. Validation loss is monitored separately because training accuracy alone cannot detect overfitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cd13acb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_epoch(model, loader, optimizer=None):\n",
    "    training = optimizer is not None\n",
    "    model.train(training)\n",
    "    total_loss = total = correct = 0\n",
    "    for x, y in loader:\n",
    "        x, y = x.to(DEVICE), y.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "        if optimizer: optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "        with torch.set_grad_enabled(training):\n",
    "            logits = model(x)\n",
    "            loss = criterion(logits, y)\n",
    "            if optimizer:\n",
    "                loss.backward(); optimizer.step()\n",
    "        total_loss += loss.item() * y.size(0)\n",
    "        correct += (logits.argmax(1) == y).sum().item()\n",
    "        total += y.size(0)\n",
    "    return total_loss / total, correct / total\n",
    "\n",
    "history = []\n",
    "best_loss = float(\"inf\"); best_state = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
    "for epoch in range(5):\n",
    "    tr_loss, tr_acc = run_epoch(model, train_loader, optimizer)\n",
    "    va_loss, va_acc = run_epoch(model, val_loader)\n",
    "    history.append((tr_loss, tr_acc, va_loss, va_acc))\n",
    "    if va_loss < best_loss:\n",
    "        best_loss = va_loss; best_state = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
    "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}: train loss {tr_loss:.4f}, acc {tr_acc:.3f} | val loss {va_loss:.4f}, acc {va_acc:.3f}\")\n",
    "model.load_state_dict(best_state)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "78b2b4e2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Plot learning curves and reflect\n",
    "\n",
    "A widening gap between training and validation performance can indicate overfitting. The project comparison found that unfreezing too many layers (Layer3 + Layer4 + classifier) produced a 79.75% test result, below the frozen-head baseline (83.14%). The more constrained Layer4 + classifier Experiment 3 was selected as the candidate, with final test metrics to be independently re-evaluated."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "75f57941",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "epochs = range(1, len(history)+1)\n",
    "plt.plot(epochs, [r[1] for r in history], marker=\"o\", label=\"train accuracy\")\n",
    "plt.plot(epochs, [r[3] for r in history], marker=\"o\", label=\"validation accuracy\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Epoch\"); plt.ylabel(\"Accuracy\"); plt.title(\"Learning curves\"); plt.legend(); plt.show()\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
